    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d316-a2">

                <pb facs="0461" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg373"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 146.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Merchants’ Exchange</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">No. 134 East
                                Bay Street, Charleston, S. C.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1892-03-09"><hi rendition="#italic">March 9,
                                1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Inclosed find New York check for $110,
                    which I am instructed to forward to you as a subscription of the “Merchants’
                    Exchange” of this city for the Russian sufferers. The exchange would
                    respectfully request that this contribution be forwarded with all convenient
                    dispatch to the American minister at St. Petersburg for proper distribution.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jno. M. Baker</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary Merchants’
                    Exchange.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
